.TH "SOPLOS-WELCOME-LIVE" "1" "2026-11-17" "Soplos Linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
soplos-welcome-live \- Welcome screen of the Soplos Linux live session
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B soplos-welcome-live
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B soplos-welcome-live
is the welcome screen of the Soplos Linux live session. Built with Tauri 2,
Rust, and Svelte, it works on Xfce (Tyron), KDE Plasma (Tyson) and GNOME
(Boro), on X11 and Wayland. It is organized in five sections:
.IP \[bu] 2
.B Home:
the edition, the processor, the memory, the graphics card and the storage of
the machine, and shortcuts to the other sections.
.IP \[bu]
.B Language:
changes the language and the keyboard layout of the system, moves the user
folders to their new names and restarts the session.
.IP \[bu]
.B Install:
launches the installer of the live session and shows what to check before
starting: the internet connection, the boot mode, the disks and the power.
Which installer it is, and where it is, is read from
.IR /usr/share/soplos-welcome-live/installer.json .
.IP \[bu]
.B Rescue:
repairs an installed system in plain language: the computer does not start,
a forgotten password, a failure after an update. It finds the installed
systems by itself, BTRFS subvolumes included, and mounts the boot, EFI and
home partitions the system's own
.I /etc/fstab
names. The advanced option opens a terminal inside the installed system.
.IP \[bu]
.B Tools:
GParted, the hardware information, the screen resolution of the session
(X11 and Plasma) and NumLock for the installed Tyron system.
.P
The interface is available in English, Spanish, German, French, Italian,
Portuguese, Romanian and Russian. It starts in the system language and falls
back to English.
.P
The window never runs as root. The live user runs the system commands with
.BR sudo (8)
without a password, and GParted is opened through
.BR pkexec (1).
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B F1
About.
.TP
.B F5
Reload the page, except while a job is running.
.TP
.B Ctrl+I
Show or hide the notes of the page (Rescue).
.TP
.B Ctrl+Tab, Ctrl+Shift+Tab
Next or previous page.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/soplos-welcome-live/installer.json
The installer of the live session: its name, the paths to try, the
environment variables and whether it needs root.
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/org.soplos.welcomelive.desktop
Present when the screen is shown at the start of the session.
.TP
.I /mnt/chroot
Where the installed system is mounted while it is repaired.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sudo (8),
.BR pkexec (1),
.BR chroot (8),
.BR gparted (8)
